hypotheses.statement:
There are positive integers $k_m$ and a constant $\gamma>0$ for which the numbers $L_m$ in <a href="#sal:multipliers" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="sal:multipliers">[sal:multipliers]</a> are positive and satisfy the following properties. Set $$D=\frac{10}{\log\beta},\qquad
 K_m=\left\lceil2b_m+DL_m\right\rceil\quad(m\ge2).$$ Then $A_m\ge1$ for every $m$, and $$\begin{aligned}
 K_m\le k_{m+1}\le e^{1.9L_m},\qquad
 L_{m+1}&\ge1.75L_m &&(m\ge2),\label{sal:growth-initial}\\
 \log K_m\le .75L_m,\qquad
 L_{m+1}&\ge2.1L_m &&(m\ge3).\label{sal:growth} 
\end{aligned}$$ Moreover, $$\label{sal:cosine-floor}
 |\cos(\pi u_{m,j})|\ge\gamma
       \quad(m\ge1,\ j\in\mathbb Z),$$ and, for $m\ge2$, $$\label{sal:small-errors}
 2\delta_m\le\frac{\gamma}{2\pi},\qquad
 \beta^{b_m-k_{m+1}}\le e^{-10L_m}
                       \le\frac{\gamma}{2\pi}.$$

For the sequence in Lemma <a href="#sal:construction" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="sal:construction">12</a>, $S_m=o(L_m)$. Furthermore, with $\eta=.01$, for $m\ge2$ and $n\ge0$, $$\label{sal:total-loss}
 \sum_{j\le n}f(u_{m,j})
       \le(2+\eta)S_m+Cn\delta_m^2.$$

Set $$S_*=\left(1+\frac{2x_*^4}{1-x_*^2}\right)^{18}
       \left(1+\frac{2x_*^3}{1-x_*^2}\right)-1.
 \label{np:pattern-cost}$$ Then $S_*<0.081$, and $$\begin{gathered}
 \sum_{\substack{d\text{ admissible}\\o(d)>0}}x_*^{o(d)}\le S_*,
 \qquad \eta_i x_*^2\le S_*/3,\\
 \frac{\overline\eta}{1-S_*/3}<0.101,
 \qquad \overline\eta=\frac1{21}\sum_{i\in B_q}\eta_i.
 \end{gathered}
 \label{np:damping-estimates}$$

For uniformly distributed words $a\in\{0,1\}^N$, $$\Pr\left\{\sum_{i\in J_N}\log F_i(x(a))>0.000220N\right\}
 \longrightarrow1.
 \label{np:typical-gain-bound}$$

